    <briefdescription>
<para>Deprecated clock reading. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The v5.0.1 class of the two readings kept by <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated_1ga53a6bc7f86b15378c8296b3647e7013f" kindref="member">detail::timestamps</ref></computeroutput>, restored for the applications that used it directly; the framework no longer uses it, since <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1stopwatch" kindref="compound">stopwatch</ref></computeroutput> keeps the readings as <computeroutput>timespec</computeroutput> members. The timings are internal; use <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1stopwatch" kindref="compound">stopwatch</ref></computeroutput> instead.</para>
<para>A zero <computeroutput>timespec</computeroutput> means that the clock was not read, or that the platform has no clock.</para>
<para>The data member is <computeroutput>protected</computeroutput>, as in v5.0.1, so that the existing derived classes can still access it. <xrefsect id="deprecated_1_deprecated000097"><xreftitle>Deprecated</xreftitle><xrefdescription><para>the timings are internal (since 6.0.0)</para>
